 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive BACnet MS/TP option card",
 "applies_to": "Yaskawa A1000, P1000, iQpump1000, U1000, FP605 and iQpump605 drives fitted with the SI-B3 BACnet MS/TP option card.",
 "summary": "The SI-B3 is a plug-in card that puts Yaskawa 1000-series and FP605/iQpump605 drives on BACnet MS/TP. Its fixed object list mirrors the drive's Modbus registers: analog and digital I/O, run/fault/reset commands, frequency and PID setpoint references, output monitors, fault and status flags, and later energy, run-time and fault-code objects. AV29/AV30 give generic access to any drive parameter.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Option software VST800265+ for AV31-AV34, VST800266+ for AV35-AV42 and BI28-BI29",
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects named Not Used (AI3-AI5, AV31, AV32, AV41, BI10-BI27, BI30) are left out.",
  "Drive-dependent object names: AV33 is Drive kWh on A1000, P1000, iQpump1000, FP605 and iQpump605 but Drive kWh Consumed on U1000; AV34 is Drive kWh Produced on U1000 and Not Used AV34 on the other drives; AV39 is Drive HOA Status on A1000, FP605 and iQpump605 but Drive Control Status on U1000, P1000 and iQpump1000. The names listed here are the A1000-family names except AV34 (U1000 only).",
  "AV1, AV4 and AV5 are packed command words; don't combine them with the single-bit objects they duplicate.",
  "Frequency units follow the drive's o1-03 display setting.",
  "Each description gives the drive Modbus register where the manual lists one."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive Option BACnet MS/TP Installation & Technical Manual, Model SI-B3",
  "doc_number": "TOEP YAICOM 22B",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TOEPYAICOM22&cmd=documents&documentName=TOEPYAICOM22.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Fit the SI-B3, set the MS/TP address in F6-45, the baud rate in F6-46 and the device instance in F6-48/F6-49, and power-cycle. Set b1-01 = 3 and b1-02 = 3 (Option PCB) so BACnet supplies the frequency reference and run command. Write BV1 RUN FWD and AV2 Frequency Command, read BV13/BV16 and AV10/AV12/AV13, and reset faults with BV4.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "RUN FWD",
    "why": "Start/stop from the BMS (drive)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2",
    "name": "Frequency Command",
    "why": "Frequency reference, units per o1-03"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 4",
    "name": "FAULT RESET",
    "why": "Reset a tripped drive"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 13",
    "name": "RUN-STOP",
    "why": "Running status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 15",
    "name": "READY",
    "why": "Drive ready to run"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10",
    "name": "Output Frequency",
    "why": "Output frequency, units per o1-03"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 12",
    "name": "Output Current",
    "why": "Motor amps"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 13",
    "name": "Output Power",
    "why": "Drive power in kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 16",
    "name": "FAULT",
    "why": "Any active drive fault"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 40",
    "name": "Last Drive Fault",
    "why": "Most recent fault code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "b1-01 Frequency Reference Selection 1 = 3 (Option PCB) and b1-02 Run Command Selection 1 = 3 (Option PCB). The defaults differ by drive model. BV5 COM NET and BV6 COM CNTRL (COM/LOCAL) are also provided.",
  "heartbeat": "When the drive loses the option link it raises bUS (Option Communication Error) and acts per F6-01: 0 ramp to stop, 1 coast, 2 fast stop, 3 alarm only, 4 alarm and run at d1-04, 5 alarm and ramp stop (4 and 5 only on some drives). F6-04 sets the bUS detection delay and F7-16 a communication-loss timeout in tenths of a second (both need option software VST800265+). F6-14 = 1 resets the bUS fault automatically when communication returns.",
  "remote_sensors": "AV3 PID Setpoint lets the BMS write the PID setpoint; BO4 Ref Sel: PID Setpoint (or AV5 bit 1) selects it.",
  "setup": [
   "F6-45 sets the MS/TP MAC address (0-127, default 1).",
   "F6-46 sets the baud rate, 1200 to 115200 bps (default setting 3 = 9600 bps).",
   "Device instance = F6-48 (low word) + F6-49 (high word), in hex; default 1. Example: 1234 is F6-48 = 4D2H, F6-49 = 0.",
   "F6-47 sets the drive transmit wait time (5-65 ms).",
   "Up to 127 drives per MS/TP segment; an EPICS file is available from Yaskawa."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "F6-01 settings 3 and 4 keep the drive running after a communication fault.",
   "BV56 Parameter Enter writes EEPROM; don't use it cyclically.",
   "Several objects only exist with newer option software (VST800265 / VST800266).",
   "AV39 Drive HOA Status does not work on iQpump1000, FP605 or iQpump605."
  ]
 },
